vely. The decrease in restructuring and integration costs for the three months ended September 30, 2026 and 2025 were primarily due to a decrease in integration and conversions related costs associated with the Amundi US acquisition.\nNine months ended September 30, 2026 compared to September 30, 2025. Restructuring and integration costs for the nine months ended September 30, 2026 and 2025 were $6.7 million and $25.4 million, respectively. The decrease is due to the same factors discussed in the quarterly section.\nInterest Income and Other Income\nThree months ended September 30, 2026 compared to September 30, 2025. Interest income and other income/(expense) was income of $0.1 million and $4.9 million for the three months ended September 30, 2026 and 2025, respectively. The decrease is primarily due to a decrease in the net unrealized fair value of deferred compensation plan investments over the comparable period.\n"}
