red to September 30, 2025. The effective tax rate for the three months ended September 30, 2026 and 2025 was 26.3% and 25.3%, respectively. The higher effective tax rate in 2026 is mainly due to an increase in non-deductible expenses.\nNine months ended September 30, 2026 compared to September 30, 2025. The effective tax rate for the nine months ended September 30, 2026 and 2025 was 25.3% and 26.8%, respectively. The year-over-year decrease in the effective tax rate is primarily driven by an increase in excess tax benefits on share-based compensation.\nSupplemental Non\u2011GAAP Financial Information\n"}
